C Code Develop is a compact C/C++ development environment with project management, header file references, and local code execution.
For coding enthusiasts and computer science students, it includes data structure projects that you can run and modify.
Write and run C/C++ projects on your device, or export a project to compile and run on your computer. The app provides a local C/C++ runtime; see the in-app API documentation for supported headers, functions, and extensions. For safety reasons, inline assembly and some other unsafe syntax are not supported.
Organize project files in nested folders, and rename, move, or delete files and folders. Build artifacts appear directly in the project.
Keep local learning notes with notebooks, search, images, rich text editing, and automatic saving. Write the title and body in one editor. Open linked code locations from notes on the home screen, or view and create linked notes from the current code file.
Browse and publish Community posts, reply to discussions, view messages and profiles, and share images, videos, and projects.
1. The editor supports code completion, automatic formatting, and long-press access to documentation.
2. The terminal supports stdin and stdout. Programs can use fopen() for file I/O within the project.
